Package: @PKG@
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Homepage: https://github.com/mahmadmujtaba/easysearch
Bugs: https://github.com/mahmadmujtaba/easysearch/issues
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: xdg-utils
Suggests: ffmpeg
Conflicts: everything-linux (<< 0.12)
Replaces: everything-linux (<< 0.12)
Provides: everything-linux
Multi-Arch: foreign
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: Instant file and content search for Linux
 EasySearch searches file names and file contents while you type,
 across your whole filesystem, and keeps its index up to date in realtime as
 files are created, renamed, changed or deleted.
 .
 It is a lightweight native application (Rust + egui): no database, no runtime
 and no web view. Queries understand globs, several terms, exclusions and
 regex; content search uses the embedded ripgrep engine and always reads files
 live rather than serving stale results.
 .
 This package installs the combined app + search-engine binary
 (easysearch), the scriptable CLI (easysearch-cli) and a headless engine
 (easysearch-daemon), plus a desktop entry, an AppStream metainfo file and the
 application icons.
 .
 The engine runs as a child process of the app and is reached over private
 pipes; nothing listens on the network, so there is no endpoint to expose.
